+	Definition~\ref{def:field-point-sandwich}. Its mean consistency defect
+	between opposite placements is at most $C_0(\eps+\sqrt{\eps})$ by
+	Lemma~\ref{lem:point-sandwich-estimates}.
+	For each $(x,z)$, apply the orthonormalization theorem with explicit
+	constant (Lemma~\ref{lem:ortho-explicit-constant}) to this POVM on
+	$\mathsf A\mathsf A'$ and its partner on $\mathsf B\mathsf A''$,
+	including the unused EPR registers in the second tensor factor.
+	This produces a projective measurement on the same first local space.
+	Apply the theorem again with the two parties reversed to obtain Bob's
+	projective measurement. Concavity of $t^{1/4}$ and finite Jensen's
+	inequality bound each mean squared distance to the sandwich by
+	$220\bigl(C_0(\eps+\sqrt{\eps})\bigr)^{1/4}$.
+	Lemma~\ref{lem:epr-cross-swap-invariance} transfers these estimates to
+	the other two placements.
+
+	The triangle inequality now follows the comparisons
+	$Q_1\approx R_1\approx (ZX)_1\approx (XZ)_2$ from
+	Lemma~\ref{lem:point-sandwich-estimates}. Commuting the last two factors
+	using Lemma~\ref{lem:field-point-commutation} gives the second ordered
+	product, and the comparison $(ZX)_2\approx R_2\approx Q_2$ gives
+	self-consistency. This argument applies to every directed pair of
+	opposite placements. For $0\le\eps\le1$, all errors are bounded by
+	$K\eps^{1/8}$ for a universal $K$. For $\eps\ge1$, the squared distance
+	between the relevant families is at most $4$: POVMs satisfy the
+	square-summability bound of Lemma~\ref{lem:sandwich-povm-square-sum},
+	and the ordered products of two projective measurements satisfy the
+	corresponding equality. Enlarging $K$ covers this range as well.
+	Thus $\delta_Q(\eps)=K\eps^{1/8}$ gives all three conclusions.
+
+	This proves the stated measurement construction without using the source's
+	intermediate binary refinements and quantum linearity construction.
+	The zero-state padding needed by that source proof remains the separate
+	import issue in Remark~\ref{rem:linearity-import} and
+	\cite{gap:qpbt_linearity-theorem-quotation}.
 \end{proof}

